//! task: write
//! ask: Declare an interface and implement it for a struct.
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §4.4, §8.6
//! explain: `interfacies Name { ... }` declares the member signatures; `interfacies Name in T { ... }` implements them for `T`. A trait's declared rows are a ceiling on every implementation, checked at each implementation head: an implementation whose capability mark exceeds the trait's is `EXS-E0510`. Here neither declares a row, so the implementation may draw nothing.

structura Duplex { n: u32 }

interfacies Contabilis {
    functio numera(x: Duplex) -> u32
}

interfacies Contabilis in Duplex {
    functio numera(x: Duplex) -> u32 {
        redde x.n;
    }
}
